35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The numbers reveal a restless tide, with costs shifting greatly between seasons. More concerning is that our payments have lagged, suggesting that uncertainty in the amount creates a hesitation to pay. We must find stability.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"That's a very important point, Servas. I've noticed that when the amounts change unexpectedly, it creates tension. I'm worried that our current way of handling payments is actually hurting our relationships and causing these delays.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found out that some rooms use way more electricity than others, especially with heaters and computers. Also, some rooms are colder because they don't get sun. It's not fair if someone pays the same but has a cold room.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"Stability is exactly the problem. The bills are all over the place—February was nearly 30,000 yen while August was under 10,000. It's a rollercoaster. Plus, installing sub-meters would cost 34,000 yen per room. That's way too expensive.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,I... I looked into other ways of doing this. One house spent forty minutes just logging readings and splitting costs by hand. And the template I tried... it required keying in every single invoice. It seems like a lot of work.,"{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"It is clear that precision comes with a price, both in money and in time. If we strive for perfect fairness, we may sacrifice the peace and simplicity that make a home a sanctuary.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"I agree, Servas. Daisuke's findings about the other house show that too much detail can be exhausting. If the process is a chore, it only adds to the stress and the risk of late payments.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Servas"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,"But if we don't do something, the people with the cold rooms or the low electricity use might still feel sad. Can't we find a way to be fair without it being too hard?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minato, ""fair"" doesn't mean spending a fortune. We can't drop over 150,000 yen just to install meters. We need a solution that handles those massive seasonal swings without costing us a month's rent upfront.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with Midori. If the process is too exhausting, it'll just be a burden for whoever does it. I'm worried that a very precise system might take up too much of someone's evening.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"Perhaps we should consider a system that encourages a spirit of generosity rather than one of strict accounting. If we focus too much on the cents, we may forget the warmth of our companionship.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, I agree. If we focus too much on strict accounting, we might end up treating each other like debtors instead of friends. We need a system that feels effortless and doesn't lead to accusations.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,"I understand, but I'm worried that if we just ignore the differences, the people who use less will still feel it's not right. Is there a way to be generous but also honest about the usage?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Minato, honesty is fine, but not at the cost of our bank accounts. We can't ignore the spikes, but we also can't afford a fancy technical fix. We need a budget that actually works year-round.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think we should avoid anything that requires a lot of manual data entry. If it's too tedious, the person managing it will just get stressed, and that's not good for anyone.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Servas,,"Let us remember that a home is not a business. If we create a system of strict surveillance, we may find ourselves shivering in silence to avoid a fee. We must choose a path of trust.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I completely agree. If we start monitoring each other too closely, we'll lose the trust that makes this house a home. Let's choose a method that prioritizes our peace of mind over perfect precision.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I don't want us to be like a business, but I also don't want anyone to feel like they are carrying someone else's burden. Can we find a middle ground that is honest but still kind?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"Look, we can be ""kind"" and ""trusting"" all we want, but that doesn't pay the bills. We need a system that smooths out those wild seasonal spikes so we aren't blindsided every winter. Let's just pick something practical.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I just hope we pick something that doesn't take hours to calculate. If it's too much work, it'll just be a burden for one person. Let's please choose the simplest option possible.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
